r the  film does not yet have a release date  Downey has great comedy chops something  we've known about him since the early  days of his career when he was playing  supporting roles in John Hughes films  like weird science he's got more recent  opportunities to show off those skills  thanks to films like chef and due date  sometime soon he'll be flexing his  comedy muscles in a big way yet again  with a role in all-star weekend the  directorial debut of his the soloist  co-star Jamie Foxx Foxx is the writer  director and star of the film which  follows two friends as they make it from  their home in Indiana to the NBA  all-star game in Los Angeles while  constantly battling each other as fans  of LeBron James and Steph Curry  respectively all-star weekend does not  have an announced release date yet and  as of late 2018 Fox was still looking  for the right distributor for the  project back in 2016 it was reported  that Downey would star in a new  miniseries from HBO following a  reimagined version of criminal defense  attorney Perry Mason from the CBS  television series starring Raymond Burr  which ran from 1957 to 1966  you didn't kill Thompson but you did mr.  Welles  set in 1930s Los Angeles the miniseries  is set to focus on the characters origin  story when the project was initially  announced true detective creator NIC  pizzolatto was also on board to write  the miniseries things have changed  significantly in the last three years  but Perry Mason is still happening  Downey is still very much involved  though he will no longer star in the  series Downey has instead stepped back  into the role of executive producer on  the series alongside his wife and  producing partner Susan Downey the  American star Matthew Rhys has instead  been cast in the title role he may be  done playing Tony Stark  but Robert Downey jr. journey as a  world-changing mogul may be just  beginning Downey appeared at Amazon's  remorse conference in June 2019 and in  the midst of a 20-minute talk about his  life career and interest in technology  and the environment he announced a major  new initiative in April of 2020 Downey  will launch the footprint coalition an  organization that will work to improve  the environment using advanced  technologies like artificial  intelligence and nanotechnology  basically Downey's playing Tony Stark in  real life he said during the  announcement between robots and  nanotechnology we could clean up the  planet significantly if not totally in  ten years at this point we still don't  know exactly what the footprint  Coalition will do first or what  technologies that we'll use to achieve  its goals at the moment the organization  is little more than a sparse website  with an option to sign up for a  newsletter but if our DJ is involved  it's likely to make plenty of headlines  in the years to come check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  MCU stars are coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

